[32m+[m[32m## Persistence and integration limits[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe existing backend has only process-local in-memory repositories. F04 follows[m
[32m+[m[32mthat convention. Requests, catalogue, reservations, and payment tracking reset on[m
[32m+[m[32mrestart. Uploaded evidence files are local; metadata does not survive a restart.[m
[32m+[m[32mDurable deployment needs database persistence and a receipt-file retention policy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChecks and mutations run synchronously in one Node process. Version checks prevent[m
[32m+[m[32mstale/concurrent updates within that process, including simultaneous payment[m
[32m+[m[32mapproval. These guarantees do not extend across multiple backend processes. A future[m
[32m+[m[32mdatabase adapter needs transactions, unique payment/idempotency constraints, atomic[m
[32m+[m[32mworker reservations, and booking conflict enforcement. No unrelated persistence[m
[32m+[m[32minfrastructure was introduced.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExisting worker availability permits one active job at a time. Assignment reserves[m
[32m+[m[32mthe worker until first completion or cancellation before start, including the time[m
[32m+[m[32mspent waiting for estimates and appointments. Completed appointment windows remain[m
[32m+[m[32munavailable until their scheduled end. A calendar supporting multiple future jobs,[m
[32m+[m[32mworker reassignment, post-start cancellation/disputes, and actual gateway integration[m
[32m+[m[32mwould be separately scoped work. Existing user deletion/relocation rules were not[m
[32m+[m[32mredesigned by this feature.[m
